title: Dynamic Headlamp Auto-Leveling (Pitch & Acceleration Compensation)
raw_community_title: Dynamic Headlamp Leveling (DHL)
category: Lighting
platform: F-150 Lightning
model_years: '2022'
trim: Lariat / Platinum (Equipped with Onboard Scales & Suspension Height Sensors)
source_sheet: Euro Kuga Mk3.5 / Ranger Platinum / Mustang S650 Comparison & Livnitup
  Master Database
status: untested
notes: 'UNTESTED / EXPERIMENTAL: Enables Dynamic Headlamp Auto-Leveling (m2_DHL_Enable
  and m2_DHL_Mode = dynamic)

  to automatically adjust vertical headlamp aim during acceleration, braking, and
  payload/towing squat.


  IMPORTANT HARDWARE REQUIREMENT: Only for 2022 F-150 Lightnings equipped from the
  factory with front

  and rear suspension ride-height sensors (Onboard Scales / Smart Hitch). Ford deleted
  physical suspension

  height sensors on 2023+ Lightnings; enabling this on a truck without height sensors
  will trigger a missing

  leveling sensor DTC. Because the Lightning''s height sensors report via the VDM
  over CAN rather than direct

  analog wiring to the HCM, m2_DHL_Input (734-01-02 xxxx xxx*) is set to 1 (CAN Input).


  NOTE ON HCM CHECKSUMS: All HCM edits must be written as exact nibble values (never
  relative offsets). Because the HCM uses a secondary calibration CRC at 734-11-01,
  an external checksum calculator is required — reach out to Firn on the F-150 Lightning
  Forum or 14th Gen F-150 Forum to discuss.'
steps:
- module: HCM
  address: 734-01-01
  notes: 'Must be entered as exact nibble values. An external HCM checksum calculator
    is required for 734-11-01 — reach out to Firn on the F-150 Lightning Forum or
    14th Gen F-150 Forum to discuss.'
  targets:
  - mask: xxx* xxxx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    # Bit positions preserved for future AsBuiltPro HCM CRC calculator support:
    # bits:
    # - bit: 0
    #   action: 1
    #   feature_name: m2_DHL_Enable (DHLE)
    #   target_state: DHLE Leveling ON
  - mask: xxxx x*xx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    # Bit positions preserved for future AsBuiltPro HCM CRC calculator support:
    # bits:
    # - bit: 0
    #   action: 1
    #   feature_name: m2_DHL_Mode (DHLM)
    #   target_state: DHLM dynamic
- module: HCM
  address: 734-01-02
  notes: 'Must be entered as exact nibble value 1 (CAN Input). An external HCM checksum
    calculator is required for 734-11-01 — reach out to Firn on the F-150 Lightning
    Forum or 14th Gen F-150 Forum to discuss.'
  targets:
  - mask: xxxx xxx* xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    # Bit positions preserved for future AsBuiltPro HCM CRC calculator support:
    # bits:
    # - bit: 0
    #   action: 1
    #   feature_name: m2_DHL_Input (DHLI)
    #   target_state: DHLI Leveling On - CAN Input
- module: LDCMA
  address: 6F6-01-01
  targets:
  - mask: x*xx xxxx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    bits:
    - bit: 0
      action: 1
      feature_name: LDM_Leveling_Cfg (LDMLC)
      target_state: LDMLC LDM Leveling present
- module: LDCMB
  address: 6F7-01-01
  targets:
  - mask: x*xx xxxx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    bits:
    - bit: 0
      action: 1
      feature_name: LDM_Leveling_Cfg (LDMLC)
      target_state: LDMLC LDM Leveling present
recipe_version: '1.1'
